\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b\par
CASE OVERVIEW:\b0  You have been given a system that has been used for some illegal activity were the user accessed confidential files that the user was not supposed to access. The system has two user accounts which are the main suspects involved in this case ("joker" and "IEUser"). You are required to provide answers to all the questions below by providing evidence (proof) with details and screenshots. Remember: SCREENSHOT OR IT DID NOT HAPPEN ;)\par

\pard\sl276\slmult1\par
Question 1: What is the hash value for the given forensic image?\par
Question 2: Which user account was used to access some confidential documents?\par
Question 3: Explain in detail what proof do you have to support your answer?\par
Question 4: Did the user access the confidential files from a local drive or network location?\par
Question 5: What proof do you have to support your answer?\par
Question 6: List all the files that were accessed with full paths.\par
Question 7: Provide two different evidence to prove that those files were truly accessed.\par
Question 8: Which application was used to open any of the confidential document(s)?\par
\b The next three questions are related to the image with the text "AnotherPassword4U" found inside the user's home directory.\b0\par
Question 9: What is the full path to the files of interest? \par
Question 10: What is the Volume Serial Number where the file exists?\par
Question 11: What are the Modified, Accessed, and Creation (MAC) timestamps in UTC for the file?\par
\b The DCode.exe application was used by one of the users. Provide evidence to the next four questions below, but, be careful, this is a tricky question!!!\b0\par
Question 12: Which user do you think ran the application and what evidence do you have to support your hypothesis?\par
Question 13: How many times was it used?\par
Question 14: When was it last used?\par
Question 15: Where was the application located (full path)?\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
Good luck!\par
